`WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated in Android API 30 and no longer functions in .NET 10's default edge-to-edge mode. Here are two approaches:

## Option 1 — Quick fix: use `AdjustPan`

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
[Activity(WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustPan)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

This scrolls the whole window up so the focused input stays visible. It works but doesn't resize your `CollectionView`/message list.

## Option 2 — Recommended: listen to `WindowInsets` (edge-to-edge)

This properly resizes your layout when the keyboard appears, which is what you want for a chat screen.

**1. In your `MainActivity.cs`, apply an insets listener:**

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        var rootView = Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!;

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Use the larger of keyboard or nav-bar bottom inset
            var bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

**2. Keep your XAML layout simple — no special flags needed:**

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" ... />

    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

**Key points:**
- The `Ime()` inset type gives you the keyboard height
- When the keyboard closes, `imeInsets.Bottom` returns to `0` and the nav-bar inset takes over
- This replaces the old `Resize` behavior with the modern Android `WindowInsets` API
- On **iOS**, `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` handles this automatically — no extra code needed
